<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/16fad9e42386> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Taylor Swift fans scammed by fake Le Creuset endorsement" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3364" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/21aef25d8076> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Touretzky notes that there's no rewinding the clock on deepfake technology." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3368" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/23dbf92cc2ab> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In October, actor Tom Hanks took to Instagram to warn fans and followers about a fake dental plan advertisement that was using his image and likeness as part of the promotion." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3370" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/27fd8ca5c5a6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The outlet reports that the fake promotional videos featured an uncanny Swift lookalike that was created with AI technology to replicate her appearance and voice." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3369" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/29e518324a88> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Le Creuset is not involved with Taylor Swift for any consumer giveaway." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3370" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2a3574fbd320> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Scammers used artificial intelligence technology to craft a synthetic version of the singer's voice, the New York Times reported Tuesday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2b173deb2762> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "No, Taylor Swift is not giving away Le Creuset cookware — it’s a scam" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3368" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2b75facf4eef> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Siwei Lyu, a computer science professor who runs the Media Forensic Lab at the University at Buffalo." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3359" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2bab7da6ba25> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Taylor Swift Is the Latest Victim of an AI Deepfake as Meta Pulls False Advertisement" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3370" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/30dfa467616b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tom Hanks and CBS Mornings host Gayle King have similarly been used in AI scams, per CBS." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3369" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/41c19b13b390> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "King recently shared a statement to her Instagram account denying claims she is affiliated with the fake weight loss ads circulating the internet with her likeness and told followers not to \"be fooled by these AI videos.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3369" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/44de25f54745> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to The New York Times, unidentified scammers used artificial intelligence and Taylor Swift's likeness to endorse a fake Le Creuset cookware giveaway to steal money and data." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3369" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4ee3bfc07213> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After becoming aware of the scam, Meta removed the advertisement and Le Creuset confirmed that the ads were fake." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3370" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5428e3aac367> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Though Taylor is, indeed, a fan of Le Creuset, she has no formal deal with the luxury cookware brand despite how it appeared in online videos." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3369" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/566e8ea11191> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Le Creuset scam campaign was probably created using a text-to-speech service, Dr. Lyu said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3359" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/58905b9116ba> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Meta spokesperson told TODAY.com that the ad has been removed from their platforms." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3367" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/63872bdcfdeb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Taylor Swift fans swindled by AI-generated Le Creuset ad scam" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3360" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6aa7887b9904> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Coffindaffer acknowledged the challenges posed by scammers operating from foreign jurisdictions, making it challenging for law enforcement agencies, including the FBI, to take effective action." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3360" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6f69da1e4c46> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Last year, when a sharp uptick in fake celebrity ads began plaguing the internet, USA Today shared a guide for spotting AI-generated videos that explained red flags to look out for." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7180d930bf3e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "AI-generated fake advertisements are making the rounds on social media again, this time using the voice and likeness of Taylor Swift promising free Le Creuset cookware sets." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7751" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/77a0666a0c8e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The campaign also ran on TikTok." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3359" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7cd5150c563d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Siwei Lyu, a computer science professor who runs the Media Forensic Lab at the University at Buffalo, told the New York Times." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3366" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8af9095d2fe2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In recent ads posted on Meta, artificial intelligence technology helped create a synthetic version of Taylor Swift's voice, which was paired with footage of her and clips of Le Creuset Dutch ovens." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3359" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/954b6157f05e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3359] 2 bills introduced in Congress last year --- the Deepfakes Accountability Act in the House and the No Fakes Act in the Senate --- would require guardrails such as content labels or permission to use someone's voice or image." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3359" .

